  "finalText": "T-1041 (\"VPN drops for the Berlin sales team\") has been triaged. This is based on the worker's report; I had no way to check the system myself. The worker says it re-read the ticket afterwards and all three changes had saved.\n\n- **Severity: sev3.** The ticket is for the VPN and affects one team, and the escalation matrix grades that as sev3. The requester's seniority and the nine people affected don't change the grade, because the matrix decides severity.\n- **Deadline: 2026-03-17T17:20:00Z.** The ticket had no deadline. It was triaged at 09:20Z by the service desk clock, and sev3 has a 480-minute response target, so the deadline is 17:20Z.\n- **Assigned to: E-301 Yuki Sato.** The network-primary rotation owns the VPN. Yuki Sato is on call for that rotation when the deadline falls, on a shift from 08:00 to 20:00Z. The ticket's status changed from new to open.\n\nNo other ticket was changed, and nothing conflicted with the handbook.\n\nThe matrix gives sev3 no escalation rotation. If the outage spreads to a whole department or the company, the ticket's impact scope and severity would have to be raised before it could be escalated.",
